1792118722-33ed4542.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1792118722-33ed4542.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1792119021-d7b44d76.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1792119021-d7b44d76.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1792119021-d7b44d76.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p>I love <a href=\"https://adamfuhrer.com\">these digital illustrations by Adam Fuhrer</a>; he calls them <a href=\"https://adamfuhrer.com#t=chromatic%20aberration\">chromatic aberrations</a>. It was difficult to narrow them down to the few favorites above. I posted about Fuhrer’s pen plotted art <a href=\"https://kottke.org/24/03/warped-bendy-pen-plots\">a couple of years ago</a>…I like the direction he’s taking this.\n</p>\n \n\n        \n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Adam%20Fuhrer\">Adam Fuhrer</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/art\">art</a></p>\n        \n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"d295f00e45b6e0eb1d9946adf41207584d8eaa60928dbc95a328eec031558524","category":"Sites"}